name: sim.createIkElement
description: Creates an IK element.
luaSynopsis: sim.createIkElement(int ikGroupHandle,int options,int[] intParams,float[] floatParams=nil)
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. ikGroupHandle: the handle to an IK group which will contain this IK element.
2. options: bit-coded options:
3. bit 0 set (1): the element is inactive
4. intParams: an array of 4 integer parameters:
5. intParams[0]: the handle of the tip dummy.
6. intParams[1]: the handle of the base object, or -1 for none (i.e. world).
7. intParams[2]: the handle of an object that will represent an alternative base for constraint evaluation, or -1 if the the constraints should be evaluated relative the the base object.
8. intParams[3]: the IK constraints.
9. floatParams: an optional array of 4 double parameters (i.e. array can be nullptr):
10. floatParams[0]: the linear precision.
11. floatParams[1]: the angular precision.
12. floatParams[2]: the position weight.
13. floatParams[3]: the orientation weight.
14. reserved: reserved. Set to nullptr.
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
